# THE GRAPHS THIS MODEL COMPOSES, AS THE LANE SETS OF ONE POOL. One row per graph: what its nodes
# are, what its edges are, and what a cycle in it means.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ A `VALUES` LITERAL, BECAUSE IT IS A CONTRACT. Derived from the tree it could never report
#    that a graph has nothing behind it, and the claimant row is exactly that case: it is declared
#    here and supplies no edges at all, which is the finding rather than an omission.
#
# ⭐⭐ THEY ARE THREE LANE SETS AND NOT THREE LANES, AND THE DIFFERENCE IS MEASURED. A `laneSet` is
#    a partition claimed exhaustive, so three LANES would put every composition in exactly one.
#    169 of 220 compositions touch more than one graph: a relation reading a part AND its factor is
#    in the layer graph and the unit graph, and that is what a factor IS. BPMN permits several lane
#    sets over one process for exactly this reason.
#
# ⛔ AND THREE LANE SETS CANNOT ALL BE THE CONTAINMENT. An inclusion tree gives each node ONE
#   parent, so only one of these can be the nesting a diagram draws; the others need showing some
#   other way. That is why `examples/diagramming/main.rs` takes the graph as a SLOT rather than picking
#   one silently, and why a caller that names none does not run.
-- the three graphs this model composes, as data an emitter chooses between.
SELECT * FROM (VALUES
  ('layers',    'a layer, keyed (filing, layer)', 'a part: F : layer -> layer',
                'a MISFILED PARTITION. The cells were one cell',              'checks/layers_move_together'),
  ('units',     'a unit',                          'a conversion: phi : unit -> unit',
                'EXPECTED, and required to CLOSE: the weights on it must vanish, so a potential exists',
                                                                              'checks/conversion_cycle_does_not_close'),
  ('claimants', 'a claimant: software, an agent, a role, a person',
                '⛔ delegation, and NOTHING FILES IT',
                'unknown. Not "nobody is accountable": mutual signing authority is a legitimate cycle',
                                                                              NULL)
) AS g(graph, node_is, edge_is, a_cycle_is, governed_by)
